Thu Nov 26 09:12:33 UTC 2026 - Tomoki Fujikawa <presire2@gmail.com>

- Update to 1.4.3:
  * Security hardening following the openSUSE security review
    (boo#1288229):
    + directories opened by the D-Bus service must now be reached
      through a trusted chain (root-owned, not writable by group or
      other) by default
    + the nearest existing ancestor of the log directory is verified
      before the directory is created, and the full chain is
      re-checked before the log file is opened
    + the service exits on idle timeout only when no reply, pending
      polkit authorization, restore or timer operation is outstanding
    + the number of pending polkit authorizations is bounded
    + requests to create a missing directory with mode 0 are rejected
  * New D-Bus signal authorizationGranted, sent only to the calling
    connection; the GUI uses it to show "Waiting for
    authentication..." and never for access decisions
  * SELinux: allow connecting to systemd-userdb sockets when NSS
    resolves user and group names
  * Fix binding loops on the settings page

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 28 04:40:23 UTC 2026 - Tomoki Fujikawa <presire2@gmail.com>

- Update to 1.4.2 (no changelog entries were added for 1.3.4 to
  1.4.1, so those releases are summarized here as well):
  * Security fixes (fixed upstream):
    + 1.4.2: when running as root, restore refuses to write beneath
      directories in which a user other than the owner can rename
      entries (group/other write bits or ACLs), preventing directory
      swap attacks that redirect a restore onto another user's files
    + 1.4.2: snapshot trees and restore destinations must be reached
      through root-owned directories not writable by other users;
      symlinks in snapshot paths are no longer followed
    + 1.4.2: Unicode bidirectional control characters in displayed
      paths and change records are replaced to prevent spoofing
    + 1.4.1: restore plans require diff-view authorization and are
      limited per user; progress/completion signals go only to the
      plan owner; expired plans are cleaned up automatically
    + 1.4.1: setuid/setgid bits and file capabilities are not applied
      when file ownership cannot be restored
    + 1.4.1: the GUI refuses to start as root and rejects instance
      handoff from other users
    + 1.3.10: legacy one-shot restore D-Bus methods removed; all
      restores use the staged single-authorization restore plan
    + 1.3.10: stricter validation of restore destinations, config
      names and values; per-user and global restore plan limits;
      restore signals no longer carry file paths or error details
    + 1.3.10: deletion during restore never follows symlinks or
      crosses mount boundaries; special files are not opened for
      reading; hardened service log and single-instance guard
    + 1.3.9: fix record-boundary injection via newlines in paths or
      descriptions; fix symlink escape in restore read helpers;
      re-validate staged restore entries at commit time
    + 1.3.7: staged multi-file restore authorized exactly once
      against a frozen manifest (polkit-gobject-1 used directly)
    + 1.3.4: remaining live-path restore operations migrated to
      dirfd-based no-follow helpers
  * User-visible changes:
    + Qt 6.5 or later is now required (was 6.2)
    + D-Bus API: staged restore plan methods added in 1.3.7, legacy
      one-shot restore methods removed in 1.3.10
    + Pre-snapshot bookkeeping moved to the user's data directory
  * New features:
    + 1.4.0: Settings tab (cleanup and space limits, background
      comparison, Btrfs quota), systemd timer management, creation
      and deletion of Snapper configurations, read-only Filesystem
      tab with Btrfs space usage and subvolume list, bulk snapshot
      deletion, important flag and user data on snapshot creation,
      grouped Pre/Post pairs, theme following the system scheme
    + 1.3.8/1.3.9: restore based on the Pre/Post snapshot diff
    + 1.3.8: main window size and maximized state are remembered
    + 1.3.4: add manual page
  * Fixes:
    + 1.4.2: empty values shown as "undefined" with Qt 6.12; German
      and Japanese translations; desktop entry no longer declares
      that the application accepts files
    + 1.4.1: restore records after cancellation, error message when
      the snapshot list cannot be loaded, header overlapping tab bar
    + 1.3.9: commas in descriptions no longer corrupt the snapshot
      list (RFC 4180 CSV)
- Correct License tag to GPL-2.0-or-later, matching upstream
- Add BuildRequires: pkgconfig(polkit-gobject-1), scdoc, cmake(Qt6Qml)
  and require Qt 6.5; package the new manual page

